Z||000003||Oreif||07-07-2001||11:18 AM||||Mount amp.<P>Hook a red 10 gage wire from battery to amp +12V in. <P>At the battery insert a 20amp fuse in a waterproof fuse holder.<P>Hook a black 10 gage wire from ground to the nearest spot on the frame. If mounting behind the seat, the seat frame rail bolt works great.<P>Hook up speakers noting which side is + and -. Usually there is a + sign on the speaker or a red dot. Make sure both speakers are wired the same.<P>From the stereo, Run a pair of RCA cables to the RCA inputs of the amp. If there are 2 sets out of the stereo use the rear outputs.<BR>On the back of the stereo there is a "remote" wire (sometimes called "pwr ant")<BR>This wire runs all the way to the amp and gets hooked to the "remote" terminal. (This is what turns the amp on when the stereo is on)<P>Once it's hooked up, Turn on the radio and on the amp is a "Gain" adjustment. I usually turn the gain all the way down then turn the radio volume all the way up. Slowly turn the gain on the amp up until the music starts to distort. (It will be very loud). Then turn the volume of the radio down. This now sets the amp level so that the stereo system puts out a clean sound at all volume levels without distorting speakers and/or amp.<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">     <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 07-07-2001).]||||reg||1
